1
00:00:09,109 --> 00:00:10,744
Nice dancing.

2
00:00:10,810 --> 00:00:13,046
It's been so long. You're good too.

3
00:00:13,847 --> 00:00:15,448
I won't lose to you.

4
00:00:28,294 --> 00:00:29,162
Hey!

5
00:00:29,229 --> 00:00:30,563
What happened?

6
00:00:30,630 --> 00:00:31,531
What is this?

7
00:00:59,759 --> 00:01:02,929
- 1, 2, 3, 4.
- 1, 2, 3, 4.

8
00:01:02,996 --> 00:01:06,099
- 1, 2, 3, 4.
- 1, 2, 3, 4.

9
00:01:06,166 --> 00:01:09,469
- 1, 2, 3, 4.
- 1, 2, 3, 4.

10
00:01:10,036 --> 00:01:11,971
Here I go.

11
00:01:12,472 --> 00:01:15,075
- Shake your hips.
- Shake your hips.

12
00:01:15,141 --> 00:01:18,278
- Shake your fans.
- Shake your fans.

13
00:01:18,344 --> 00:01:20,747
That's good.

14
00:01:21,948 --> 00:01:23,983
Let's go.

15
00:01:24,517 --> 00:01:27,153
1, 2, 3... Mambo!

16
00:01:28,188 --> 00:01:31,591
What's this organized group movement?

17
00:01:32,192 --> 00:01:33,359
So obnoxious.

18
00:01:35,295 --> 00:01:37,497
Let's go down.

19
00:01:41,367 --> 00:01:42,335
You should join.

20
00:01:54,981 --> 00:01:56,249
Here we go.

21
00:01:58,785 --> 00:02:01,621
1, 2, 3... Mambo!

22
00:02:21,741 --> 00:02:24,577
Move, you're in the way.

23
00:02:25,145 --> 00:02:27,080
No. You're in the way.

24
00:02:27,413 --> 00:02:29,449
Are you alright?

25
00:02:30,717 --> 00:02:33,286
Oh no. Cardiac arrest.

26
00:02:36,689 --> 00:02:39,058
- Get an ambulance. You get the AED.
- Yes.

27
00:02:39,125 --> 00:02:40,860
- You take her shoes off.
- Yes.

28
00:02:40,927 --> 00:02:43,129
- You get ice. Lots.
- Yes.

29
00:02:43,196 --> 00:02:45,398
Wave with your fans.

30
00:02:45,465 --> 00:02:46,666
- Hello?
- Yes!

31
00:02:48,601 --> 00:02:50,637
What are you doing? You too.

32
00:02:51,771 --> 00:02:54,040
- You too, old man.
- Old man?

33
00:02:55,875 --> 00:02:57,143
Forgive me.

34
00:03:10,123 --> 00:03:12,525
Misa!

35
00:03:12,592 --> 00:03:14,394
Misa!

36
00:03:14,460 --> 00:03:16,029
She has a runny nose.

37
00:03:16,095 --> 00:03:17,864
Could be acute myocarditis.

38
00:03:17,931 --> 00:03:21,100
She almost has fulminant myocarditis.

39
00:03:21,167 --> 00:03:23,403
She needs PCPS fast.

40
00:03:23,469 --> 00:03:24,637
Switch with me.

41
00:03:25,205 --> 00:03:27,140
You're a doctor? Please come.

42
00:03:27,207 --> 00:03:29,175
No, just a passing dancer.

43
00:03:29,242 --> 00:03:30,176
Take care of her.

44
00:03:38,751 --> 00:03:40,853
He was absolutely correct.

45
00:03:40,920 --> 00:03:42,689
And he's good at skipping.

46
00:03:42,755 --> 00:03:44,624
That dancer's good.

47
00:03:44,691 --> 00:03:47,093
I said he's too obnoxious.

48
00:03:47,160 --> 00:03:48,161
Yeah.

49
00:03:48,228 --> 00:03:51,598
<i>This is a story about</i>
<i>a maverick female doctor.</i>

50
00:03:52,432 --> 00:03:54,200
<i>In 2014,</i>

51
00:03:54,267 --> 00:03:57,136
<i>medical establishments collapsed</i>
<i>and became more corrupt.</i>

52
00:03:57,503 --> 00:03:59,772
<i>Medicine, which handles lives,</i>

53
00:03:59,839 --> 00:04:03,209
<i>had strayed away from what it should be.</i>

54
00:04:03,276 --> 00:04:06,813
We will now begin
the preoperative conference.

55
00:04:07,280 --> 00:04:09,649
The first case is Ms. Shizuko Suita,

56
00:04:09,716 --> 00:04:11,217
65 years old.

57
00:04:11,718 --> 00:04:14,053
The second case is Ms. Nanami Kotozuka,

58
00:04:14,120 --> 00:04:15,455
70 years old.

59
00:04:16,022 --> 00:04:17,824
The diagnosis is

60
00:04:17,890 --> 00:04:20,293
gastric carcinoma stage III-A.

61
00:04:21,127 --> 00:04:23,563
However, despite these conditions,

62
00:04:23,930 --> 00:04:26,499
Japan announced to export

63
00:04:26,566 --> 00:04:28,034
state of the art medical

64
00:04:28,101 --> 00:04:30,737
services as a growth strategy.

65
00:04:31,170 --> 00:04:32,305
Sir.

66
00:04:33,172 --> 00:04:35,341
I, the Unified Director, will explain.

67
00:04:35,408 --> 00:04:39,979
Healthcare entered an era
of the strong preying on the weak.

68
00:04:40,046 --> 00:04:42,882
Both have 5cm tumors by

69
00:04:42,949 --> 00:04:45,084
the greater curvature of the stomach.

70
00:04:45,151 --> 00:04:47,887
I propose distal gastrectomy

71
00:04:47,954 --> 00:04:49,822
and the Billroth I method.

72
00:04:49,889 --> 00:04:52,592
Kaji and Hara will be the surgeons.

73
00:04:53,092 --> 00:04:54,127
Yes, sir.

74
00:04:54,193 --> 00:04:55,328
I object.

75
00:04:56,796 --> 00:04:59,098
- Demon, again?
- What?

76
00:05:00,199 --> 00:05:01,901
I'd use Billroth II

77
00:05:01,968 --> 00:05:04,404
and reconstruct better than them.

78
00:05:04,470 --> 00:05:06,272
- What?
- Let me do it.

79
00:05:08,708 --> 00:05:09,942
Dr. Daimon.

80
00:05:11,277 --> 00:05:12,912
I cannot let you operate.

81
00:05:12,979 --> 00:05:13,813
Why not?

82
00:05:13,880 --> 00:05:15,181
JUNKO SHIRAKI, HEAD NURSE

83
00:05:16,449 --> 00:05:17,383
Please come in.

84
00:05:24,057 --> 00:05:25,024
Hello.

85
00:05:27,160 --> 00:05:28,561
Dr. Fujikawa!

86
00:05:29,996 --> 00:05:32,465
That's not needed. Please sit.

87
00:05:33,433 --> 00:05:34,334
Yes, sir.

88
00:05:35,134 --> 00:05:36,002
Who's that?

89
00:05:36,669 --> 00:05:38,004
You don't know?

90
00:05:41,541 --> 00:05:42,675
Let me introduce him.

91
00:05:43,443 --> 00:05:47,246
This is Dr. Kiyoshiro Fujikawa,

92
00:05:47,914 --> 00:05:50,350
who transferred from
Seikyo University Hospital.

93
00:05:50,750 --> 00:05:51,918
I'm Fujikawa.

94
00:05:51,984 --> 00:05:53,086
Nice to meet you.

95
00:05:56,956 --> 00:06:01,994
As Seikyo University's
Unified Surgical Director,

96
00:06:02,061 --> 00:06:03,796
he published many articles.

97
00:06:03,863 --> 00:06:07,367
He is a world-renowned doctor.

98
00:06:07,433 --> 00:06:11,871
The other day,
the American medical magazine AMJ...

99
00:06:11,938 --> 00:06:13,339
That's not needed either.

100
00:06:18,578 --> 00:06:20,179
Strangely intimidating.

101
00:06:25,551 --> 00:06:26,652
I see.

102
00:06:29,555 --> 00:06:30,823
You're right.

103
00:06:32,325 --> 00:06:36,062
With Billroth I, the stomach may become

104
00:06:36,129 --> 00:06:38,131
too small to connect to the duodenum.

105
00:06:39,031 --> 00:06:41,033
Even if it does, the suture could

106
00:06:41,801 --> 00:06:43,436
rupture from too much tension.

107
00:06:44,137 --> 00:06:47,407
But with Billroth II, ruptures are rare,

108
00:06:48,174 --> 00:06:51,477
and chances of
gastritis or cancer are the same.

109
00:06:52,612 --> 00:06:55,982
It's the best reconstruction method.

110
00:06:56,048 --> 00:06:56,916
Dr. Ebina.

111
00:06:57,984 --> 00:07:01,320
This is his article published in the AMJ.

112
00:07:01,387 --> 00:07:02,555
BILROTH I VS. BILROTH II VS. ROUX-EN-Y...

113
00:07:04,924 --> 00:07:06,459
Therefore,

114
00:07:06,826 --> 00:07:09,362
I also believe Billroth II would be best.

115
00:07:11,264 --> 00:07:13,065
He's the same as me.

116
00:07:13,132 --> 00:07:14,400
Dr. Daimon.

117
00:07:15,802 --> 00:07:18,204
You still don't understand.

118
00:07:18,271 --> 00:07:19,338
What?

119
00:07:19,405 --> 00:07:21,307
He is the ideal doctor

120
00:07:21,374 --> 00:07:23,242
that this hospital seeks.

121
00:07:24,644 --> 00:07:26,112
No matter how skilled one is...

122
00:07:26,712 --> 00:07:30,283
Depending on intuition or casual ideas

123
00:07:31,217 --> 00:07:34,520
will cause healthcare to lose its trust.

124
00:07:35,521 --> 00:07:36,355
Yes, sir.

125
00:07:37,990 --> 00:07:40,359
What's he saying?

126
00:07:45,698 --> 00:07:46,899
Get her out.

127
00:07:46,966 --> 00:07:49,168
He's trying to show his presence.

128
00:07:51,137 --> 00:07:52,171
Say "Yes, sir!"

129
00:07:52,839 --> 00:07:53,940
Yes, sir!

130
00:07:54,006 --> 00:07:55,107
Yeah, yeah.

131
00:07:55,174 --> 00:07:56,342
Wait.

132
00:08:00,480 --> 00:08:02,248
Mr. Tendo, I have a proposition.

133
00:08:04,550 --> 00:08:06,185
May Dr. Daimon and I be in charge

134
00:08:06,786 --> 00:08:10,223
of the 2 patients' operations?

135
00:08:18,064 --> 00:08:18,998
Very well.

136
00:08:22,468 --> 00:08:28,541
I will ask Dr. Fujikawa
and Dr. Daimon to be the surgeons.

137
00:08:28,608 --> 00:08:29,842
Thank you.

138
00:08:30,743 --> 00:08:34,280
You sure are quick to make decisions, sir.

139
00:08:35,448 --> 00:08:38,618
But I can do it by myself.

140
00:08:38,684 --> 00:08:43,155
<i>Then came freelance doctors</i>
<i>who don't belong to any hospitals.</i>

141
00:08:43,656 --> 00:08:47,093
<i>In other words, maverick doctors.</i>

142
00:08:48,027 --> 00:08:50,630
You have the power of 100 men.

143
00:08:50,696 --> 00:08:52,431
The East is done for.

144
00:08:52,498 --> 00:08:53,766
That's it?

145
00:08:53,833 --> 00:08:56,168
When I walk, at least 100 follow.

146
00:08:57,403 --> 00:08:59,071
Wait.

147
00:08:59,672 --> 00:09:01,007
She's alone?

148
00:09:01,541 --> 00:09:03,609
<i>For example, this woman.</i>

149
00:09:04,443 --> 00:09:07,847
<i>She hates groups,</i>
<i>authority, and being controlled.</i>

150
00:09:08,347 --> 00:09:13,152
<i>Her medical license and experience</i>
<i>are her only weapons.</i>

151
00:09:14,220 --> 00:09:16,656
So you're the dancer from last night.

152
00:09:16,722 --> 00:09:19,191
I'm shocked. It's destiny.

153
00:09:19,659 --> 00:09:20,927
- Move.
- Ms. Daimon.

154
00:09:21,661 --> 00:09:23,129
I hear you're good.

155
00:09:23,796 --> 00:09:26,065
I hear you're really fast at surgery.

156
00:09:27,033 --> 00:09:29,802
Want to fight me?

157
00:09:30,603 --> 00:09:32,838
A race to see who's quicker.

158
00:09:32,905 --> 00:09:34,006
Not interested.

159
00:09:34,073 --> 00:09:36,709
You accept? How brave.

160
00:09:37,777 --> 00:09:39,845
If you lose, you get in line.

161
00:09:40,746 --> 00:09:42,582
- I won't do that.
- A race it is.

162
00:09:43,716 --> 00:09:44,850
Open the way.

163
00:09:45,284 --> 00:09:46,185
Yes, sir!

164
00:09:50,356 --> 00:09:51,958
Too obnoxious.

165
00:09:54,160 --> 00:09:55,661
I'll crush that woman.

166
00:09:56,963 --> 00:09:57,797
Yes, sir!

167
00:09:59,398 --> 00:10:02,068
<i>Surgeon Michiko Daimon,</i>

168
00:10:03,135 --> 00:10:06,439
<i>also known as Doctor-X.</i>

169
00:10:18,985 --> 00:10:21,387
SHIZUKO SUITA NANAMI KOTOZUKA

170
00:10:22,254 --> 00:10:26,025
Surgery risks include pancreatic fistula

171
00:10:26,092 --> 00:10:29,428
or ruptured sutures by the duodenum stump.

172
00:10:29,495 --> 00:10:31,530
It sounds hard.

173
00:10:31,597 --> 00:10:33,432
Take this! Bomb!

174
00:10:33,499 --> 00:10:35,935
Be quiet.

175
00:10:39,839 --> 00:10:41,073
Don't worry.

176
00:10:41,607 --> 00:10:44,477
The duodenum stump

177
00:10:44,543 --> 00:10:46,112
will be reinforced as well.

178
00:10:47,513 --> 00:10:50,816
Dr. Fujikawa appears in
many medical magazines.

179
00:10:50,883 --> 00:10:53,285
I said not needed.

180
00:10:53,719 --> 00:10:55,921
Basically, I'm an unbelievable doctor

181
00:10:55,988 --> 00:10:58,190
you won't find anywhere else.

182
00:10:59,358 --> 00:11:02,695
Aren't you glad you got a good doctor?

183
00:11:02,762 --> 00:11:04,430
I'm very thankful.

184
00:11:04,497 --> 00:11:05,398
Thank you.

185
00:11:05,464 --> 00:11:06,298
Thank you.

186
00:11:06,365 --> 00:11:09,135
Let's go to the amusement park.

187
00:11:09,201 --> 00:11:10,436
Yes, let's go.

188
00:11:10,503 --> 00:11:12,738
No lying, okay?

189
00:11:14,774 --> 00:11:17,076
This isn't much...

190
00:11:17,143 --> 00:11:19,145
I can't accept these things...

191
00:11:19,211 --> 00:11:20,713
It's nothing.

192
00:11:20,780 --> 00:11:22,848
I can't accept it.

193
00:11:22,915 --> 00:11:24,583
Please don't trouble me.

194
00:11:24,650 --> 00:11:26,385
Too obnoxious.

195
00:11:27,153 --> 00:11:28,421
Then I'll accept.

196
00:11:30,856 --> 00:11:31,991
I'm Daimon, your doctor.

197
00:11:32,858 --> 00:11:35,127
It's loud, so change rooms.

198
00:11:36,228 --> 00:11:37,196
Yes.

199
00:11:38,597 --> 00:11:41,534
If anything, you should change doctors.

200
00:11:41,901 --> 00:11:43,636
She's a part-timer.

201
00:11:43,703 --> 00:11:45,705
Don't say that.

202
00:11:45,771 --> 00:11:47,873
Sorry, don't worry about that.

203
00:11:48,374 --> 00:11:49,208
Let's go.

204
00:11:53,379 --> 00:11:55,848
NANAMI KOTOZUKA, PATIENT

205
00:11:55,915 --> 00:11:58,651
You're a part-timer?

206
00:11:59,285 --> 00:12:00,352
Freelancer.

207
00:12:00,953 --> 00:12:02,555
Unbelievable.

208
00:12:03,689 --> 00:12:07,960
Even big hospitals
like this have part-time doctors?

209
00:12:11,797 --> 00:12:14,667
- You're a part-timer too?
- Not me.

210
00:12:16,235 --> 00:12:19,505
I came to Japan's best hospital,

211
00:12:20,473 --> 00:12:22,641
and I get a part-timer.

212
00:12:24,810 --> 00:12:26,245
If I can change rooms,

213
00:12:26,612 --> 00:12:28,914
maybe I really will change doctors.

214
00:12:28,981 --> 00:12:31,217
You'll die if it's not me.

215
00:12:32,485 --> 00:12:33,652
Dr. Daimon!

216
00:12:33,719 --> 00:12:35,621
How dare you say that.

217
00:12:35,688 --> 00:12:37,890
Your attitude is unacceptable.

218
00:12:37,957 --> 00:12:40,025
Do not make the patient worry...

219
00:12:40,092 --> 00:12:42,194
You're obnoxious too.

220
00:12:50,970 --> 00:12:53,072
Dr. Fujikawa challenged Daimon.

221
00:12:56,242 --> 00:12:57,076
Well,

222
00:12:58,477 --> 00:13:00,279
just because he can write articles,

223
00:13:00,346 --> 00:13:02,348
doesn't mean he can operate.

224
00:13:02,782 --> 00:13:03,749
Look at Daimon.

225
00:13:04,283 --> 00:13:05,451
She can't write

226
00:13:05,518 --> 00:13:07,286
a case report, let alone an article.

227
00:13:10,022 --> 00:13:11,857
Excuse me.

228
00:13:11,924 --> 00:13:14,860
I'll be in the next room,
so I came to say hi.

229
00:13:16,195 --> 00:13:17,530
Dr. Ebina,

230
00:13:18,164 --> 00:13:20,566
it seems you're called
the Unified Director,

231
00:13:20,633 --> 00:13:22,635
but don't go unifying things.

232
00:13:23,435 --> 00:13:24,670
Now that I'm here,

233
00:13:24,737 --> 00:13:27,973
the East and West will be separate.

234
00:13:30,543 --> 00:13:32,444
Dr. Kaji, Dr. Hara.

235
00:13:32,945 --> 00:13:35,014
I've heard about you two.

236
00:13:35,748 --> 00:13:38,117
I hear you're great doctors.

237
00:13:38,784 --> 00:13:40,686
How about dinner sometime?

238
00:13:41,887 --> 00:13:42,721
Bye now.

239
00:13:51,864 --> 00:13:54,667
How much do you get

240
00:13:54,733 --> 00:13:56,235
from Dr. Ebina a month?

241
00:13:56,802 --> 00:13:57,636
Huh?

242
00:13:58,103 --> 00:14:00,940
- You're his girl, right?
- Of course not.

243
00:14:01,006 --> 00:14:02,007
Oh no!

244
00:14:02,074 --> 00:14:03,876
He's a director,

245
00:14:03,943 --> 00:14:06,245
but his secretary isn't his lover?

246
00:14:06,745 --> 00:14:08,747
What a strange man.

247
00:14:10,749 --> 00:14:12,184
It's not much.

248
00:14:13,152 --> 00:14:15,354
This is all I got today.

249
00:14:15,855 --> 00:14:17,623
Eat something nice.

250
00:14:24,730 --> 00:14:26,265
Not bad.

251
00:14:26,332 --> 00:14:27,566
TOMOKO SEKIGAHARA, SECRETARY

252
00:14:27,633 --> 00:14:29,001
KANBARA DOCTOR AGENCY

253
00:14:29,068 --> 00:14:31,971
That dancer was Kiyoshiro Fujikawa.

254
00:14:32,404 --> 00:14:35,307
Quite the man has come.

255
00:14:35,708 --> 00:14:39,011
I hear his articles are a work of god.

256
00:14:39,078 --> 00:14:40,980
He's that great?

257
00:14:41,046 --> 00:14:42,414
For example, that man.

258
00:14:42,481 --> 00:14:45,618
He loves groups,
authority, and being controlled.

259
00:14:46,018 --> 00:14:47,887
With his license,

260
00:14:47,953 --> 00:14:50,589
his flashy performances
are his only weapons.

261
00:14:50,656 --> 00:14:51,490
Gross!

262
00:14:51,557 --> 00:14:52,892
Disgusting.

263
00:14:52,958 --> 00:14:54,126
Disgusting.

264
00:14:54,193 --> 00:14:56,362
This is one of his greatest weapons.

265
00:15:00,699 --> 00:15:03,135
Yes. He uses people.

266
00:15:03,202 --> 00:15:06,739
He sweet talks his workers

267
00:15:06,805 --> 00:15:09,241
and flatters his superiors.

268
00:15:09,308 --> 00:15:11,310
A typical salary worker.

269
00:15:11,377 --> 00:15:14,446
Guys like him move up in organizations.

270
00:15:14,513 --> 00:15:16,749
With Fujikawa's smooth talk,

271
00:15:16,815 --> 00:15:19,151
Dr. Kaji and Dr. Hara

272
00:15:19,218 --> 00:15:21,253
will be knocked out in no time.

273
00:15:22,254 --> 00:15:23,589
Knock out!

274
00:15:23,656 --> 00:15:24,490
What?

275
00:15:24,556 --> 00:15:27,293
Ron. 8,000 points.

276
00:15:27,359 --> 00:15:28,994
What...

277
00:15:37,836 --> 00:15:39,772
Dr. Fujikawa!

278
00:15:40,639 --> 00:15:45,010
Fujikawa. Fujikawa.

279
00:15:45,077 --> 00:15:46,679
Okay, okay.

280
00:15:46,745 --> 00:15:48,514
It's my new appointment celebration.

281
00:15:48,580 --> 00:15:50,516
Drink up.

282
00:15:57,923 --> 00:15:59,892
Drink up.

283
00:15:59,959 --> 00:16:02,027
Cheers!

284
00:16:03,963 --> 00:16:05,664
Looks fun over there.

285
00:16:06,865 --> 00:16:08,100
We're scouting today.

286
00:16:08,167 --> 00:16:11,403
We must report this to Dr. Ebina.

287
00:16:14,373 --> 00:16:17,876
Thanks for coming.

288
00:16:18,477 --> 00:16:19,878
I'm honored to be invited.

289
00:16:20,279 --> 00:16:22,815
Honestly, is there anything good

290
00:16:22,881 --> 00:16:24,483
about working for Dr. Ebina?

291
00:16:26,151 --> 00:16:27,653
Of course...

292
00:16:27,720 --> 00:16:30,756
You won't move up. Neither will your pay.

293
00:16:38,497 --> 00:16:40,566
Great! Great!

294
00:16:40,632 --> 00:16:43,302
Think about it.

295
00:16:43,802 --> 00:16:45,838
Dr. Ebina takes all the great

296
00:16:45,904 --> 00:16:48,007
opportunities that come down.

297
00:16:48,073 --> 00:16:49,575
But he does nothing.

298
00:16:52,111 --> 00:16:55,647
We're doctors,
but we're just salary workers.

299
00:16:56,382 --> 00:16:58,784
You should choose
who to be loyal to based on profit.

300
00:16:59,551 --> 00:17:03,255
I believe so.

301
00:17:04,790 --> 00:17:08,327
Oh no, that wasn't needed. Just drink up.

302
00:17:08,394 --> 00:17:09,261
Thank you.

303
00:17:10,095 --> 00:17:11,497
So Dr. Fujikawa,

304
00:17:12,097 --> 00:17:15,267
I hear you'll be
racing Daimon in the surgery...

305
00:17:15,334 --> 00:17:18,604
No, no. Not a race. I'm testing her.

306
00:17:20,039 --> 00:17:23,642
Your career and fame as
a doctor are way above Daimon's.

307
00:17:24,209 --> 00:17:26,412
A part-timer can't stand a chance.

308
00:17:27,279 --> 00:17:28,313
However...

309
00:17:30,182 --> 00:17:31,150
However?

310
00:17:32,317 --> 00:17:34,853
Daimon is amazingly fast.

311
00:17:34,920 --> 00:17:38,357
Her surgery's the work of the devil.

312
00:17:39,591 --> 00:17:41,693
Even with your skills...

313
00:17:41,760 --> 00:17:43,228
I agree.

314
00:17:44,029 --> 00:17:46,632
In order to not defame your name,

315
00:17:46,698 --> 00:17:50,069
I suggest you avoid the race.

316
00:17:50,135 --> 00:17:52,037
Are you kidding me?

317
00:17:52,438 --> 00:17:55,674
She gets carried away
because you're such wimps.

318
00:17:57,342 --> 00:17:59,078
That woman is a pest.

319
00:17:59,578 --> 00:18:02,414
She must be crushed quickly, right?

320
00:18:06,085 --> 00:18:09,221
- Runa, Yuka, come here.
- Coming...

321
00:18:11,156 --> 00:18:13,659
MINEJI KATO, HEAD OF INTERNAL AFFAIRS

322
00:18:13,725 --> 00:18:16,995
Yes, sir. Yes, sir.

323
00:18:18,263 --> 00:18:21,300
That's how I became director.

324
00:18:22,401 --> 00:18:25,304
If my "Yes-sir career" is useless,

325
00:18:25,370 --> 00:18:28,373
what meaning is there to my job?

326
00:18:30,209 --> 00:18:33,145
Besides, how old is Fujikawa?

327
00:18:34,046 --> 00:18:35,080
50?

328
00:18:35,814 --> 00:18:37,449
He's a year younger than us.

329
00:18:37,516 --> 00:18:38,884
How much is he getting paid?

330
00:18:39,751 --> 00:18:41,053
How much is he getting paid?

331
00:18:42,020 --> 00:18:43,555
I said how much?

332
00:18:44,857 --> 00:18:46,959
More than me?

333
00:18:47,659 --> 00:18:48,827
Why?

334
00:18:50,562 --> 00:18:54,633
He's some guy from
the West that popped up.

335
00:18:56,135 --> 00:18:58,904
Why do I have to be outdone by him?

336
00:19:01,173 --> 00:19:02,307
Why?

337
00:19:03,075 --> 00:19:04,743
Say something.

338
00:19:06,445 --> 00:19:07,579
Ebina.

339
00:19:08,614 --> 00:19:10,782
Stop your babbling.

340
00:19:12,918 --> 00:19:15,020
Think doctors are great?

341
00:19:15,087 --> 00:19:19,892
You and your great processions every day.

342
00:19:20,692 --> 00:19:23,095
If you think only
doctors support a hospital,

343
00:19:23,162 --> 00:19:24,763
you're totally wrong.

344
00:19:25,264 --> 00:19:26,932
- Sorry.
- I'm the secretariat.

345
00:19:26,999 --> 00:19:28,300
I'm sorry.

346
00:19:28,367 --> 00:19:31,970
I have 3 daughters. My wife left me.

347
00:19:32,404 --> 00:19:34,706
I have loans and alimony to pay.

348
00:19:35,340 --> 00:19:38,944
I'm barely staying alive.

349
00:19:39,511 --> 00:19:43,148
She could let me off
for cheating just once.

350
00:19:43,215 --> 00:19:44,349
Right, Ebina?

351
00:19:44,416 --> 00:19:45,484
Yeah.

352
00:19:45,551 --> 00:19:51,690
I'll bow down to the ground...

353
00:19:53,458 --> 00:19:57,196
I'll lick my boss's shoes...

354
00:19:57,729 --> 00:19:59,398
To win favor.

355
00:19:59,965 --> 00:20:01,667
I'll win it all!

356
00:20:02,267 --> 00:20:03,902
What's wrong with that?

357
00:20:03,969 --> 00:20:06,605
Nothing. I'll say it too.

358
00:20:07,039 --> 00:20:08,574
I'll say it forever.

359
00:20:09,174 --> 00:20:11,610
Yes, sir. Yes, sir.

360
00:20:13,412 --> 00:20:16,181
Let's be proud, Kato.

361
00:20:17,216 --> 00:20:18,283
Ebina.

362
00:20:18,984 --> 00:20:20,285
Yes, sir!

363
00:20:27,926 --> 00:20:29,561
Hooray! "Yes, sir."

364
00:20:29,628 --> 00:20:31,496
Hooray salary workers.

365
00:20:31,563 --> 00:20:33,432
Kato, be a dog.

366
00:20:36,435 --> 00:20:39,371
Eat paper, Ebina. You're a goat.

367
00:20:42,241 --> 00:20:44,843
Ebina!

368
00:20:48,146 --> 00:20:50,482
TABLE TENNIS COURT

369
00:20:51,650 --> 00:20:53,852
Here I go.

370
00:20:53,919 --> 00:20:55,988
Ashigara.

371
00:20:56,622 --> 00:20:58,590
Nihondaira.

372
00:20:59,291 --> 00:21:01,293
Oi Matsuda.

373
00:21:01,360 --> 00:21:05,130
Dangozaka.

374
00:21:05,197 --> 00:21:08,600
No. That place is on the Chuo Expressway.

375
00:21:20,112 --> 00:21:20,946
So free...

376
00:21:21,013 --> 00:21:22,681
Hachioji.

377
00:21:23,248 --> 00:21:24,549
Too much freedom.

378
00:21:24,616 --> 00:21:26,285
Katsuura.

379
00:21:32,824 --> 00:21:33,792
I'm jealous.

380
00:21:34,693 --> 00:21:36,061
I want to be Daimon.

381
00:21:47,372 --> 00:21:48,440
Gosh!

382
00:21:48,507 --> 00:21:50,042
It sure is Japan's best hospital.

383
00:21:50,108 --> 00:21:51,643
So many cuties.

384
00:21:51,710 --> 00:21:52,944
Wow...

385
00:21:53,011 --> 00:21:54,513
Oh no,

386
00:21:54,579 --> 00:21:55,447
you're all

387
00:21:55,514 --> 00:21:57,149
so bright I can't see.

388
00:21:58,350 --> 00:22:00,352
Alright. For tomorrow's surgery,

389
00:22:00,786 --> 00:22:04,056
I'll have you and you help.

390
00:22:04,122 --> 00:22:04,956
Here.

391
00:22:05,023 --> 00:22:06,658
Really? This is expensive.

392
00:22:06,725 --> 00:22:08,026
Of course.

393
00:22:08,093 --> 00:22:10,862
- I want one.
- Me too.

394
00:22:10,929 --> 00:22:12,397
I'll give it to you.

395
00:22:16,968 --> 00:22:19,705
Dr. Fujikawa, that's not alright.

396
00:22:19,771 --> 00:22:20,939
There are work schedules.

397
00:22:21,006 --> 00:22:24,142
It's your job to have the doctors relaxed.

398
00:22:25,143 --> 00:22:26,545
This is for you.

399
00:22:27,846 --> 00:22:31,216
But don't come to my surgery.

400
00:22:31,283 --> 00:22:33,719
I'm begging you. Bye.

401
00:22:38,023 --> 00:22:39,224
Let's return these.

402
00:22:42,260 --> 00:22:44,463
Don't change the schedule.

403
00:22:44,930 --> 00:22:45,964
Yes.

404
00:22:46,531 --> 00:22:47,833
Get back to work.

405
00:22:48,166 --> 00:22:49,034
Yes...

406
00:22:50,535 --> 00:22:53,438
INFORMED CONSENT

407
00:22:58,110 --> 00:22:59,578
The surgery is at 1pm.

408
00:22:59,644 --> 00:23:02,114
Don't eat anything after dinner.

409
00:23:02,581 --> 00:23:05,050
It's a risky operation?

410
00:23:05,117 --> 00:23:07,386
Don't worry. I don't fail.

411
00:23:08,019 --> 00:23:09,454
You can fail.

412
00:23:10,155 --> 00:23:12,391
I'm single anyway.

413
00:23:12,457 --> 00:23:13,558
SIGNED: NANAMI KOTOZUKA

414
00:23:13,625 --> 00:23:15,160
EMERGENCY CONTACT

415
00:23:15,227 --> 00:23:16,561
Any family?

416
00:23:16,628 --> 00:23:19,631
No. Always been alone.

417
00:23:23,435 --> 00:23:24,870
You're single too.

418
00:23:26,738 --> 00:23:30,008
I don't smell family on you.

419
00:23:31,410 --> 00:23:33,412
Not your business.

420
00:23:35,280 --> 00:23:36,648
Remember this.

421
00:23:37,482 --> 00:23:41,219
The more skilled you are,
the more organizations reject you.

422
00:23:41,953 --> 00:23:45,190
Good ones are shot down. Especially women.

423
00:23:46,725 --> 00:23:51,263
What awaits such women
is a lonely life of retirement.

424
00:23:53,298 --> 00:23:55,033
You're lonely?

425
00:23:57,135 --> 00:23:59,237
But it was your choice.

426
00:24:00,939 --> 00:24:02,307
Don't say that.

427
00:24:03,108 --> 00:24:06,611
For a woman to be accepted, she must work.

428
00:24:06,978 --> 00:24:09,581
Even if they're shot down,
women must fight.

429
00:24:11,750 --> 00:24:12,617
What?

430
00:24:16,922 --> 00:24:18,523
Do you have a fever?

431
00:24:24,896 --> 00:24:26,164
You're like me.

432
00:24:27,666 --> 00:24:28,867
I'm sorry.

433
00:24:31,603 --> 00:24:34,239
It's nice and quiet here.

434
00:24:59,431 --> 00:25:01,566
No cheating tomorrow.

435
00:25:28,426 --> 00:25:31,229
PATIENT: SHIZUKO SUITA SURGEON: FUJIKAWA

436
00:25:45,076 --> 00:25:48,013
PATIENT: NANAMI KOTOZUKA
SURGEON: DAIMON

437
00:25:53,518 --> 00:25:54,386
We will begin...

438
00:25:54,452 --> 00:25:56,821
Distal gastrectomy.

439
00:25:56,888 --> 00:25:58,023
- Scalpel.
- Yes.

440
00:26:02,494 --> 00:26:03,995
- Scalpel.
- Yes.

441
00:26:08,333 --> 00:26:09,568
SURGERY TIME

442
00:26:14,739 --> 00:26:16,141
The gates are open.

443
00:26:16,207 --> 00:26:17,175
The race has begun.

444
00:26:19,544 --> 00:26:20,745
I have a bad feeling.

445
00:26:21,413 --> 00:26:23,515
Demon won't lose.

446
00:26:26,284 --> 00:26:27,819
- Time?
- 18 minutes.

447
00:26:27,886 --> 00:26:29,321
- Blood loss?
- 30cc.

448
00:26:36,561 --> 00:26:40,165
Right gastroepiploic artery confirmed.
Tying the root. Metzen.

449
00:26:46,538 --> 00:26:49,407
- I'll remove the omentum.
- Yes.

450
00:26:49,474 --> 00:26:50,375
2nd assistant,

451
00:26:50,442 --> 00:26:52,577
- pull the transverse mesocolon.
- Yes.

452
00:26:52,644 --> 00:26:53,778
- Forceps.
- Yes.

453
00:26:56,448 --> 00:26:58,249
Next is the vein.

454
00:26:58,316 --> 00:26:59,250
Sealing device.

455
00:26:59,851 --> 00:27:00,919
- Hurry.
- Yes.

456
00:27:12,831 --> 00:27:14,566
<i>Transverse mesorectum.</i>

457
00:27:16,568 --> 00:27:19,304
<i>Right gastroepiploic artery confirmed.</i>

458
00:27:19,371 --> 00:27:20,238
<i>- Scalpel.</i>
<i>- Yes.</i>

459
00:27:21,873 --> 00:27:22,707
<i>Give it.</i>

460
00:27:33,785 --> 00:27:36,354
Too slow.
Give me the linear stapler. Hurry.

461
00:27:36,421 --> 00:27:37,255
Yes.

462
00:27:48,233 --> 00:27:51,069
Let's tie her up. 2-0 nylon.

463
00:27:51,136 --> 00:27:51,970
Yes.

464
00:28:49,728 --> 00:28:50,628
Dr. Ebina.

465
00:28:51,896 --> 00:28:53,998
- Anything happen?
- No.

466
00:28:55,700 --> 00:28:59,304
- Daimon, you're fast. It's over?
- No, I'm taking the specimen.

467
00:29:10,215 --> 00:29:11,182
I'm done.

468
00:29:13,084 --> 00:29:15,019
Seems they're not done next door.

469
00:29:16,221 --> 00:29:19,023
How is that the work of the devil?

470
00:29:20,625 --> 00:29:22,894
Thanks for welcoming me.

471
00:29:29,100 --> 00:29:30,635
Daimon lost?

472
00:29:31,302 --> 00:29:32,771
What is she doing?

473
00:29:33,238 --> 00:29:34,139
Dr. Kaji.

474
00:29:41,713 --> 00:29:42,747
She's not done.

475
00:29:43,481 --> 00:29:46,918
Daimon, of all days, you're slow today?

476
00:29:46,985 --> 00:29:48,386
You lost.

477
00:29:48,853 --> 00:29:49,687
Daimon!

478
00:29:50,989 --> 00:29:52,090
Let me talk.

479
00:29:54,025 --> 00:29:56,361
Ms. Daimon, still not done?

480
00:29:56,427 --> 00:29:58,062
You're a bit too slow.

481
00:29:58,596 --> 00:30:01,833
I feel sorry for the old patient.

482
00:30:01,900 --> 00:30:03,668
Ah...

483
00:30:04,602 --> 00:30:07,272
The nurse is old too over here.

484
00:30:07,772 --> 00:30:09,407
I'm sorry.

485
00:30:09,474 --> 00:30:14,145
Anyway, don't rush
and do a good job. Bye now.

486
00:30:19,851 --> 00:30:21,653
Look.

487
00:30:28,560 --> 00:30:29,394
Done.

488
00:30:29,861 --> 00:30:33,998
Blood loss 150. Blood pressure 100,
pulse 60 and sinus.

489
00:30:38,970 --> 00:30:39,904
Thank you.

490
00:30:39,971 --> 00:30:41,406
Good job.

491
00:30:41,472 --> 00:30:43,074
Thank you.

492
00:30:53,651 --> 00:30:55,553
I heard she's talented,

493
00:30:55,620 --> 00:30:57,322
but she's not that good.

494
00:30:58,223 --> 00:30:59,824
You did well.

495
00:30:59,891 --> 00:31:02,293
Please look after the patient.

496
00:31:02,360 --> 00:31:05,296
Meeting the new Minister
of Health, Labour and Welfare?

497
00:31:07,699 --> 00:31:10,068
May I join you?

498
00:31:12,370 --> 00:31:13,204
Sure.

499
00:31:14,505 --> 00:31:15,340
Thank you.

500
00:31:15,406 --> 00:31:17,175
Maybe next time.

501
00:31:29,954 --> 00:31:31,222
Too slow.

502
00:31:31,289 --> 00:31:32,824
Give me the linear stapler.

503
00:31:32,891 --> 00:31:33,825
Yes.

504
00:31:35,360 --> 00:31:38,863
His speed is beyond belief.

505
00:31:38,930 --> 00:31:40,365
Great, right?

506
00:31:40,431 --> 00:31:42,100
It's not just his articles.

507
00:31:44,435 --> 00:31:46,204
Too obnoxious.

508
00:31:47,171 --> 00:31:49,307
Hey, part-timer.

509
00:31:49,374 --> 00:31:51,342
You weren't bad.

510
00:31:51,409 --> 00:31:53,311
Only 10 minutes late.

511
00:31:53,378 --> 00:31:58,082
Pretty good.
You're good. Let's shake hands.

512
00:31:59,717 --> 00:32:00,551
I won't do that.

513
00:32:06,524 --> 00:32:07,592
Don't be shy.

514
00:32:07,659 --> 00:32:09,160
It's not a shame

515
00:32:09,527 --> 00:32:11,462
if you lose to me.

516
00:32:15,466 --> 00:32:16,301
What?

517
00:32:21,205 --> 00:32:23,308
It's 5pm, so bye.

518
00:32:26,744 --> 00:32:28,479
Scary face.

519
00:32:31,449 --> 00:32:32,483
Really scary.

520
00:32:41,759 --> 00:32:43,161
Wait, Dr. Daimon.

521
00:32:44,228 --> 00:32:47,298
Aren't you mad you lost to a man like him?

522
00:32:47,365 --> 00:32:48,199
No.

523
00:32:48,266 --> 00:32:50,935
Have you no pride as a woman?

524
00:32:51,002 --> 00:32:55,873
I wasn't fighting him. Bye.

525
00:32:58,009 --> 00:33:01,813
I want good beef.

526
00:33:08,686 --> 00:33:10,321
She got money?

527
00:33:12,256 --> 00:33:13,825
That has to be it.

528
00:33:14,459 --> 00:33:16,160
The usual Daimon would never lose.

529
00:33:16,728 --> 00:33:19,464
Fujikawa bought his victory?

530
00:33:19,530 --> 00:33:21,899
Demon always goes for money.

531
00:33:23,001 --> 00:33:23,835
Fixed game?

532
00:33:23,901 --> 00:33:27,505
I should've taken
the challenge and got paid.

533
00:33:27,572 --> 00:33:28,406
Kaji.

534
00:33:29,407 --> 00:33:30,408
Oh.

535
00:33:30,908 --> 00:33:32,944
It's Daimon's fault. Not yours.

536
00:33:33,378 --> 00:33:35,346
Our lives have been ruined...

537
00:33:38,082 --> 00:33:39,217
It's all Daimon's fault.

538
00:33:42,620 --> 00:33:44,555
I'm not as ruined as you...

539
00:33:45,957 --> 00:33:47,125
Let's drink.

540
00:33:47,191 --> 00:33:48,026
Here.

541
00:33:50,361 --> 00:33:51,562
I'll get wasted.

542
00:33:53,264 --> 00:33:54,298
TABLE TENNIS COURT

543
00:33:54,365 --> 00:33:57,502
She doesn't fail?

544
00:33:57,568 --> 00:33:58,803
She won't do that?

545
00:33:58,870 --> 00:34:00,538
Do it, Demon.

546
00:34:00,605 --> 00:34:01,706
Say "Yes, sir."

547
00:34:01,773 --> 00:34:03,241
Our lives...

548
00:34:03,307 --> 00:34:04,442
Give it back.

549
00:34:07,111 --> 00:34:08,279
I drank too much.

550
00:34:12,216 --> 00:34:13,284
This is terrible.

551
00:34:13,351 --> 00:34:14,419
We can't play.

552
00:34:14,485 --> 00:34:15,353
Let's go.

553
00:34:17,422 --> 00:34:18,456
Tokyo Station.

554
00:34:18,523 --> 00:34:19,424
Mikawa-Anjo.

555
00:34:19,490 --> 00:34:20,358
Shinagawa.

556
00:34:20,425 --> 00:34:21,759
Gifu-Hashima.

557
00:34:21,826 --> 00:34:22,927
Shin-Yokohama.

558
00:34:22,994 --> 00:34:23,995
Maibara.

559
00:34:24,829 --> 00:34:26,464
You're all better now.

560
00:34:26,531 --> 00:34:28,766
Congratulations.

561
00:34:28,833 --> 00:34:30,935
I owe it to Dr. Fujikawa.

562
00:34:31,302 --> 00:34:32,603
Thank you so much.

563
00:34:33,204 --> 00:34:35,440
Congrats, Grandma.

564
00:34:36,974 --> 00:34:38,676
Congrats!

565
00:34:39,777 --> 00:34:41,345
Thank you.

566
00:34:51,222 --> 00:34:52,090
Dr. Daimon.

567
00:34:54,725 --> 00:34:55,760
It's not right.

568
00:34:57,829 --> 00:35:01,365
We had the same condition
and had surgery the same day.

569
00:35:02,500 --> 00:35:05,937
But why am I still here?

570
00:35:14,612 --> 00:35:17,515
You're not a good surgeon.

571
00:35:18,950 --> 00:35:22,553
You're just a part-timer, after all.

572
00:35:26,424 --> 00:35:28,593
Recovery speed varies.

573
00:35:28,659 --> 00:35:30,294
Even if you go home, you're alone.

574
00:35:33,164 --> 00:35:34,365
Stay a bit longer.

575
00:35:34,432 --> 00:35:35,800
Mom!

576
00:35:35,867 --> 00:35:37,135
Are you okay?

577
00:35:37,201 --> 00:35:38,236
What's wrong, Mom?

578
00:35:38,302 --> 00:35:39,670
What's the matter?

579
00:35:39,737 --> 00:35:41,572
Mom! What happened?

580
00:35:44,475 --> 00:35:45,843
Are you okay?

581
00:35:45,910 --> 00:35:47,745
Mom...

582
00:35:50,381 --> 00:35:51,749
Surgery, now.

583
00:35:51,816 --> 00:35:53,985
- Yes. Get the stretcher.
- Yes.

584
00:35:55,720 --> 00:35:57,588
Mom, Mom...

585
00:35:57,655 --> 00:35:58,756
It'll be okay.

586
00:36:08,833 --> 00:36:11,669
Don't take my patient to the surgery room.

587
00:36:11,736 --> 00:36:13,838
A blocked afferent loop.

588
00:36:13,905 --> 00:36:17,141
That's within expectation. I'll operate.

589
00:36:25,883 --> 00:36:28,519
Afferent loop repositioning.

590
00:36:28,586 --> 00:36:30,154
- Scalpel.
- Yes.

591
00:36:44,402 --> 00:36:45,836
Oh no!

592
00:36:45,903 --> 00:36:47,004
What?

593
00:36:47,071 --> 00:36:50,308
You didn't do Brown's anastomosis.

594
00:36:50,374 --> 00:36:51,976
Oh no.

595
00:36:52,043 --> 00:36:55,146
- No 14v lymph node dissection either?
- What?

596
00:36:55,213 --> 00:36:56,247
No wonder.

597
00:36:56,314 --> 00:36:58,516
Idiot. You can do that

598
00:36:58,583 --> 00:37:00,184
if something goes wrong.

599
00:37:00,251 --> 00:37:01,385
And it did.

600
00:37:01,452 --> 00:37:03,221
So I'm operating.

601
00:37:03,588 --> 00:37:07,258
Cops don't investigate
when there's no crime.

602
00:37:07,325 --> 00:37:08,292
It's not like that.

603
00:37:08,359 --> 00:37:09,594
If they get sick,

604
00:37:09,660 --> 00:37:11,162
you should operate. Got it?

605
00:37:11,229 --> 00:37:12,196
Seriously?

606
00:37:12,697 --> 00:37:14,865
Watch. I'll teach you since this

607
00:37:14,932 --> 00:37:17,435
might happen to your patient.

608
00:37:17,501 --> 00:37:19,270
- It won't.
- What?

609
00:37:19,337 --> 00:37:21,806
- Because I didn't fail.
- What?

610
00:37:21,872 --> 00:37:23,574
You're slow. Move.

611
00:37:24,408 --> 00:37:27,178
What?

612
00:37:27,245 --> 00:37:28,212
Move.

613
00:37:35,720 --> 00:37:38,522
The afferent loop is almost necrotic.

614
00:37:38,589 --> 00:37:40,057
- Pean.
- Yes.

615
00:37:41,826 --> 00:37:42,727
I'm sorry.

616
00:37:50,701 --> 00:37:52,570
- Linear stapler.
- Yes.

617
00:38:02,179 --> 00:38:03,648
- Intestinal forceps.
- Yes.

618
00:38:03,714 --> 00:38:05,283
Not the stapler?

619
00:38:05,349 --> 00:38:08,319
Brown's anastomosis.
I'll suture with my hands.

620
00:38:08,386 --> 00:38:09,420
- Hurry.
- Yes.

621
00:38:10,321 --> 00:38:11,155
Move.

622
00:38:19,730 --> 00:38:20,564
- Monopolar.
- Yes.

623
00:38:33,878 --> 00:38:35,313
- 2-0 nylon.
- Yes.

624
00:39:03,708 --> 00:39:04,775
- Cooper.
- Yes.

625
00:39:17,021 --> 00:39:18,122
Done.

626
00:39:31,769 --> 00:39:32,937
Thank you.

627
00:39:33,504 --> 00:39:34,438
Nice work.

628
00:39:34,505 --> 00:39:35,940
Thank you.

629
00:39:55,159 --> 00:39:57,595
NATIONAL ADVANCED MEDICAL CENTER

630
00:40:03,467 --> 00:40:05,669
You're Kanbara, Daimon's manager?

631
00:40:06,103 --> 00:40:07,872
Hello, Dr. Fujikawa.

632
00:40:08,305 --> 00:40:10,341
I've heard much about you.

633
00:40:10,875 --> 00:40:13,444
That you're an obnoxious dancer.

634
00:40:13,511 --> 00:40:15,045
Doctor, not dancer.

635
00:40:15,112 --> 00:40:16,280
I'm sorry.

636
00:40:16,347 --> 00:40:17,448
Let me see the bill.

637
00:40:17,948 --> 00:40:18,949
I'll take it.

638
00:40:19,817 --> 00:40:21,752
Sure. Let's go there.

639
00:40:23,254 --> 00:40:24,388
TEN MILLION YEN

640
00:40:24,455 --> 00:40:27,024
You're as cheap as I've heard.

641
00:40:27,091 --> 00:40:28,459
Our Daimon

642
00:40:28,926 --> 00:40:31,996
performed preventative treatment,

643
00:40:32,062 --> 00:40:34,131
predicting what would happen.

644
00:40:37,368 --> 00:40:38,202
Also,

645
00:40:38,736 --> 00:40:42,807
she performed surgery for you,

646
00:40:42,873 --> 00:40:45,843
who failed to do such preventative
treatment for your patient.

647
00:40:45,910 --> 00:40:46,944
Move!

648
00:40:48,212 --> 00:40:49,947
I'll suture with my hands.

649
00:40:53,651 --> 00:40:54,552
Therefore,

650
00:40:54,618 --> 00:40:57,721
I believe it's a fair price.

651
00:40:57,788 --> 00:40:58,823
Shut up.

652
00:40:59,190 --> 00:41:01,358
I didn't fail to do it. I chose not to.

653
00:41:01,859 --> 00:41:02,693
Chose not to?

654
00:41:02,760 --> 00:41:03,727
Yeah.

655
00:41:03,794 --> 00:41:05,830
I finished quickly since I didn't.

656
00:41:06,163 --> 00:41:11,035
Meaning there's that much
less stress on the patient.

657
00:41:14,305 --> 00:41:15,172
What's wrong?

658
00:41:15,239 --> 00:41:16,674
2 surgeries

659
00:41:16,740 --> 00:41:18,175
will raise hospital profit.

660
00:41:18,242 --> 00:41:20,511
The better choice is clear.

661
00:41:20,578 --> 00:41:22,079
Right, Mr. Kato?

662
00:41:23,113 --> 00:41:25,883
Are you sure that's really alright?

663
00:41:27,084 --> 00:41:28,719
By operating twice,

664
00:41:29,386 --> 00:41:32,389
you put twice the stress on the patient.

665
00:41:34,692 --> 00:41:37,361
As usual, please wire the money.

666
00:41:37,428 --> 00:41:38,429
Money?

667
00:41:42,766 --> 00:41:44,335
How much...?

668
00:41:49,440 --> 00:41:50,975
How obnoxious.

669
00:41:51,041 --> 00:41:52,510
I can't even skip.

670
00:41:56,714 --> 00:41:58,215
I understand.

671
00:41:59,817 --> 00:42:01,986
Do the usual, Ikawa.

672
00:42:06,257 --> 00:42:07,124
Mr. Tendo.

673
00:42:07,691 --> 00:42:08,759
Dr. Fujikawa.

674
00:42:10,094 --> 00:42:16,066
I believe that you now understand
the surgeon, Michiko Daimon.

675
00:42:19,270 --> 00:42:25,276
In surgeries...
Even you can't beat Michiko Daimon.

676
00:42:30,548 --> 00:42:33,918
And you even had a foolish race.

677
00:42:40,524 --> 00:42:42,026
I didn't call you

678
00:42:42,927 --> 00:42:45,296
to crush Michiko Daimon.

679
00:42:47,531 --> 00:42:49,266
It was to use her.

680
00:42:52,236 --> 00:42:54,672
Do you understand?

681
00:42:56,840 --> 00:42:58,008
To use her...

682
00:43:04,181 --> 00:43:05,749
Eat porridge for a week.

683
00:43:06,684 --> 00:43:10,254
If stomach pains
or fevers continue, come in.

684
00:43:10,888 --> 00:43:11,722
Thank you.

685
00:43:13,123 --> 00:43:15,292
You healed quicker than your neighbor.

686
00:43:16,961 --> 00:43:20,064
Maybe I'll stay a little longer.

687
00:43:20,130 --> 00:43:21,999
No one's at home, anyway.

688
00:43:23,334 --> 00:43:26,136
If you get lonely, come over for mahjong.

689
00:43:27,137 --> 00:43:29,340
Really? I'm coming.

690
00:43:30,975 --> 00:43:31,809
Bye.

691
00:43:35,145 --> 00:43:37,982
I'll carry this for you.

692
00:43:38,048 --> 00:43:40,184
- Don't forget anything.
- Thank you.

693
00:43:40,250 --> 00:43:41,518
Thank you.

694
00:43:41,952 --> 00:43:45,456
<i>She hates groups,</i>
<i>authority, and being controlled.</i>

695
00:43:45,856 --> 00:43:50,227
<i>Her medical license</i>
<i>and experience are her only weapons.</i>

696
00:43:52,029 --> 00:43:55,299
Ron! That's 16,000 points.

697
00:43:55,366 --> 00:43:56,200
What a hand!

698
00:43:56,800 --> 00:43:58,035
What!

699
00:43:58,102 --> 00:43:59,069
I'm 1st place.

700
00:43:59,136 --> 00:44:00,971
You're too strong.

701
00:44:01,438 --> 00:44:03,140
Who invited her?

702
00:44:03,207 --> 00:44:04,174
No one.

703
00:44:04,241 --> 00:44:06,710
It's still early. One more game.

704
00:44:14,151 --> 00:44:14,985
Pong.

705
00:44:15,619 --> 00:44:16,687
So, Chief.

706
00:44:17,321 --> 00:44:19,423
It's about the new Dr. Fujikawa.

707
00:44:19,490 --> 00:44:21,925
I didn't come here to talk about work.

708
00:44:22,259 --> 00:44:23,827
Pong.

709
00:44:23,894 --> 00:44:26,163
She's got a big hand again.

710
00:44:28,165 --> 00:44:29,433
But I know this.

711
00:44:29,500 --> 00:44:31,235
- A secret?
- What?

712
00:44:31,301 --> 00:44:33,937
I hate guys like him.

713
00:44:35,005 --> 00:44:37,741
I finally agree with you.

714
00:44:38,709 --> 00:44:39,977
- Ron!
- What?

715
00:44:40,044 --> 00:44:41,311
That's 32,000 points.

716
00:44:41,378 --> 00:44:43,580
You fool.

717
00:44:43,647 --> 00:44:45,149
You're too weak.

718
00:44:45,215 --> 00:44:46,083
I quit.

719
00:44:46,550 --> 00:44:48,052
Let's play again.

720
00:44:56,627 --> 00:44:58,529
I hate this woman.

721
00:44:59,196 --> 00:45:01,432
<i>Surgeon Michiko Daimon,</i>

722
00:45:01,999 --> 00:45:03,167
<i>also known as</i>

723
00:45:03,634 --> 00:45:05,202
<i>Doctor-X.</i>

724
00:46:23,847 --> 00:46:25,783
Can't my daughter get a lung?

725
00:46:25,849 --> 00:46:28,752
No donor can match an 8-year-old's body.

726
00:46:29,186 --> 00:46:32,256
For the patient,
one failure and it's over.

727
00:46:32,322 --> 00:46:34,091
I want to save her.

728
00:46:34,158 --> 00:46:37,728
I don't care about
personal or business relations.
